{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>From the Arnon to the Jabbok.</b> The land of Moab and the land of the children of Ammon are east of the land of Canaan, and the land of Sihon is between the two of them. Just as Sihon took the land of Moab from the south side, from the Jordan to the Arnon valley, so too he took from the north side the land of the children of Ammon as far as the Jabbok. Through this it was permitted to Israel, and this is what they said: Ammon and Moab were purified through Sihon." "<b>For the border of the children of Ammon was strong.</b> But from the Jabbok onward he did not conquer, for the Jabbok river, which is the border of the children of Ammon, was mighty and strong, and it separated between Sihon and the children of Ammon."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:07.238441657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}